#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.42 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:5
msgid "UI, Workflows & Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:8
msgid ""
"\"git pack-refs\" learns \"--include\" and \"--exclude\" to tweak the ref "
"hierarchy to be packed using pattern matching."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:11
msgid ""
"'git worktree add' learned how to create a worktree based on an orphaned "
"branch with `--orphan`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:15
msgid ""
"\"git pack-objects\" learned to invoke a new hook program that enumerates "
"extra objects to be used as anchoring points to keep otherwise unreachable "
"objects in cruft packs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:18
msgid ""
"Add more \"git var\" for toolsmiths to learn various locations Git is "
"configured with either via the configuration or hard-coded defaults."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:21
msgid ""
"'git notes append' was taught '--separator' to specify string to insert "
"between paragraphs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:24
msgid ""
"The \"git for-each-ref\" family of commands learned placeholders related to "
"GPG signature verification."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:28
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-index\" learned to read from named pipes as if they were "
"regular files, to allow \"git diff <(process) <(substitution)\" some shells "
"support."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:32
msgid ""
"Help newbies by suggesting that there are cases where force-pushing is a "
"valid and sensible thing to update a branch at a remote repository, rather "
"than reconciling with merge/rebase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:35
msgid ""
"\"git blame --contents=file\" has been taught to work in a bare repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:40
msgid ""
"\"git branch -f X\" to repoint the branch X said that X was \"checked out\" "
"in another worktree, even when branch X was not and instead being bisected "
"or rebased.  The message was reworded to say the branch was \"in use\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:46
msgid ""
"Tone down the warning on SHA-256 repositories being an experimental "
"curiosity.  We do not have support for them to interoperate with traditional "
"SHA-1 repositories, but at this point, we do not plan to make breaking "
"changes to SHA-256 repositories and there is no longer need for such a "
"strongly phrased warning."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:49
msgid "Performance, Internal Implementation, Development Support etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:52
msgid ""
"\"git diff-tree\" has been taught to take advantage of the sparse-index "
"feature."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:55
msgid ""
"Clang's sanitizer implementation seems to work better than GCC's.  (merge "
"d88d727143 jk/ci-use-clang-for-sanitizer-jobs later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:60
msgid ""
"The object traversal using reachability bitmap done by \"pack-object\" has "
"been tweaked to take advantage of the fact that using \"boundary\" commits "
"as representative of all the uninteresting ones can save quite a lot of "
"object enumeration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:62
msgid "discover_git_directory() no longer touches the_repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:64
msgid "\"git worktree\" learned to work better with sparse index feature."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:68
msgid ""
"When the external merge driver is killed by a signal, its output should not "
"be trusted as a resolution with conflicts that is proposed by the driver, "
"but the code did."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:71
msgid ""
"The set-up code for the get_revision() API now allows feeding options like --"
"all and --not in the --stdin mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:74
msgid ""
"Move functions that are not about pure string manipulation out of strbuf.[ch]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:77
msgid "\"imap-send\" codepaths got cleaned up to get rid of unused parameters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:80
msgid ""
"Enumerating refs in the packed-refs file, while excluding refs that match "
"certain patterns, has been optimized."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:83
msgid ""
"Mark-up unused parameters in the code so that we can eventually enable -"
"Wunused-parameter by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:86
msgid ""
"Instead of inventing a custom counter variables for debugging, use existing "
"trace2 facility in the fsync customization codepath."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:89
msgid ""
"\"git branch --list --format=<format>\" and friends are taught a new "
"\"%(describe)\" placeholder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:92
msgid ""
"Clarify how to choose the starting point for a new topic in developer "
"guidance document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:98
msgid ""
"The implementation of \"get_sha1_hex()\" that reads a hexadecimal string "
"that spells a full object name has been extended to cope with any hash "
"function used in the repository, but the \"sha1\" in its name survived.  "
"Rename it to get_hash_hex(), a name that is more consistent within its "
"friends like get_hash_hex_algop()."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:100
msgid "Command line parser fix, and a small parse-options API update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.41"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:108
msgid ""
"\"git tag\" learned to leave the \"$GIT_DIR/TAG_EDITMSG\" file when the "
"command failed, so that the user can salvage what they typed.  (merge "
"08c12ec1d0 kh/keep-tag-editmsg-upon-failure later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:114
msgid ""
"The \"-s\" (silent, squelch) option of the \"diff\" family of commands did "
"not interact with other options that specify the output format well.  This "
"has been cleaned up so that it will clear all the formatting options given "
"before.  (merge 9d484b92ed jc/diff-s-with-other-options later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:117
msgid ""
"Update documentation regarding Coccinelle patches.  (merge 3bd0097cfc gc/doc-"
"cocci-updates later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:122
msgid ""
"Some atoms that can be used in \"--format=<format>\" for \"git ls-tree\" "
"were not supported by \"git ls-files\", even though they were relevant in "
"the context of the latter.  (merge 4d28c4f75f zh/ls-files-format-atoms later "
"to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:126
msgid ""
"Document more pseudo-refs and teach the command line completion machinery to "
"complete AUTO_MERGE.  (merge 982ff3a649 pb/complete-and-document-auto-merge-"
"and-friends later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:132
msgid ""
"\"git submodule\" code trusted the data coming from the config (and the in-"
"tree .gitmodules file) too much without validating, leading to NULL "
"dereference if the user mucks with a repository (e.g.  submodule.<name>.url "
"is removed).  This has been corrected.  (merge fbc806acd1 tb/submodule-null-"
"deref-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:138
msgid ""
"The value of config.worktree is per-repository, but has been kept in a "
"singleton global variable per process. This has been OK as most Git "
"operations interacted with a single repository at a time, but not right for "
"operations like recursive \"grep\" that want to access multiple repositories "
"from a single process without forking."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:142
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The global variable has been eliminated and made into a member in\n"
"the per-repository data structure.\n"
"(merge 3867f6d650 vd/worktree-config-is-per-repository later to maint).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:145
msgid ""
"\"git [-c log.follow=true] log [--follow] ':(glob)f**'\" used to barf.  "
"(merge 8260bc5902 jk/log-follow-with-non-literal-pathspec later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:149
msgid ""
"Introduce a mechanism to disable replace refs globally and per repository.  "
"(merge 9c7d1b057f ds/disable-replace-refs later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:153
msgid ""
"\"git cat-file --batch\" and friends learned \"-Z\" that uses NUL delimiter "
"for both input and output.  (merge f79e18849b ps/cat-file-null-output later "
"to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:156
msgid ""
"The reimplemented \"git add -i\" did not honor color.ui configuration.  "
"(merge 6f74648cea ds/add-i-color-configuration-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:159
msgid ""
"Compilation fix for platforms without D_TYPE in struct dirent.  (merge "
"03bf92b9bf as/dtype-compilation-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:163
msgid ""
"Suggest to refrain from using hex literals that are non-portable when "
"writing printf(1) format strings.  (merge f0b68f0546 jt/doc-use-octal-with-"
"printf later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:166
msgid ""
"Simplify error message when run-command fails to start a command.  (merge "
"6d224ac286 rs/run-command-exec-error-on-noent later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:170
msgid ""
"Gracefully deal with a stale MIDX file that lists a packfile that no longer "
"exists.  (merge 06f3867865 tb/open-midx-bitmap-fallback later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:176
msgid ""
"Even when diff.ignoreSubmodules tells us to ignore submodule changes, \"git "
"commit\" with an index that already records changes to submodules should "
"include the submodule changes in the resulting commit, but it did not.  "
"(merge 5768478edc js/defeat-ignore-submodules-config-with-explicit-addition "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:182
msgid ""
"When \"git commit --trailer=...\" invokes the interpret-trailers machinery, "
"it knows what it feeds to interpret-trailers is a full log message without "
"any patch, but failed to express that by passing the \"--no-divider\" "
"option, which has been corrected.  (merge be3d654343 jk/commit-use-no-"
"divider-with-interpret-trailers later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:186
msgid ""
"Avoid breakage of \"git pack-objects --cruft\" due to inconsistency between "
"the way the code enumerates packfiles in the repository.  (merge 73320e49ad "
"tb/collect-pack-filenames-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:191
msgid ""
"We create .pack and then .idx, we consider only packfiles that have .idx "
"usable (those with only .pack are not ready yet), so we should remove .idx "
"before removing .pack for consistency.  (merge 0dd1324a73 ds/remove-idx-"
"before-pack later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:195
msgid ""
"Partially revert a sanity check that the rest of the config code was not "
"ready, to avoid triggering it in a corner case.  (merge a53f43f900 gc/config-"
"partial-submodule-kvi-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:199
msgid ""
"\"git apply\" punts when it is fed too large a patch input; the error "
"message it gives when it happens has been clarified.  (merge 42612e18d2 pw/"
"apply-too-large later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:204
msgid ""
"During a cherry-pick or revert session that works on multiple commits, \"git "
"status\" did not give correct information, which has been corrected.  (merge "
"a096a889f4 jk/cherry-pick-revert-status later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:209
msgid ""
"A few places failed to differentiate the case where the index is truly empty "
"(nothing added) and we haven't yet read from the on-disk index file, which "
"have been corrected.  (merge 2ee045eea1 js/empty-index-fixes later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:213
msgid ""
"\"git bugreport\" tests did not test what it wanted to test, which has been "
"corrected.  (merge 1aa92b8500 ma/t0091-fixup later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:217
msgid ""
"Code snippets in a tutorial document no longer compiled after recent header "
"shuffling, which have been corrected.  (merge bbd7c7b7c0 vd/adjust-mfow-doc-"
"to-updated-headers later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:222
msgid ""
"\"git ls-files '(attr:X)D/'\" that triggers the common prefix optimization "
"codepath failed to read from \"D/.gitattributes\", which has been "
"corrected.  (merge f4a8fde057 jc/pathspec-match-with-common-prefix later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:226
msgid ""
"\"git fsck --no-progress\" still spewed noise from the commit-graph "
"subsystem, which has been corrected.  (merge 9281cd07f0 tb/fsck-no-progress "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:231
msgid ""
"Various offset computation in the code that accesses the packfiles and other "
"data in the object layer has been hardened against arithmetic overflow, "
"especially on 32-bit systems.  (merge 9a25cad7e0 tb/object-access-overflow-"
"protection later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:237
msgid ""
"Names of MinGW header files are spelled in mixed case in some source files, "
"but the build host can be using case sensitive filesystem with header files "
"with their name spelled in all lowercase.  (merge 4a53d0d0bc mh/mingw-case-"
"sensitive-build later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:240
msgid ""
"Update message mark-up for i18n in \"git bundle\".  (merge bbb6acd998 dk/"
"bundle-i18n-more later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:244
msgid ""
"\"git tag --list --points-at X\" showed tags that directly refers to object "
"X, but did not list a tag that points at such a tag, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:249
msgid ""
"\"./configure --with-expat=no\" did not work as a way to refuse use of the "
"expat library on a system with the library installed, which has been "
"corrected.  (merge fb8f7269c2 ah/autoconf-fixes later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:256
msgid ""
"When the user edits \"rebase -i\" todo file so that it starts with a "
"\"fixup\", which would make it invalid, the command truncated the rest of "
"the file before giving an error and returning the control back to the user.  "
"Stop truncating to make it easier to correct such a malformed todo file.  "
"(merge 9645a087c2 ah/sequencer-rewrite-todo-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:260
msgid ""
"Rewrite the description of giving a custom command to the submodule.<name>."
"update configuration variable.  (merge 7cebc5bd78 pv/doc-submodule-update-"
"settings later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:264
msgid ""
"Adjust to OpenSSL 3+, which deprecates its SHA-1 functions based on its "
"traditional API, by using its EVP API instead.  (merge bda9c12073 ew/hash-"
"with-openssl-evp later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:268
msgid ""
"Exclude \".\" from the set of characters to be removed from the beginning "
"and the end of the human-readable name.  (merge 1c04cb0744 bc/ident-dot-is-"
"no-longer-crud-letter later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:273
msgid ""
"\"git bisect visualize\" stopped running \"gitk\" on Git for Windows when "
"the command was reimplemented in C around Git 2.34 timeframe.  This has been "
"corrected.  (merge fff1594fa7 ma/locate-in-path-for-windows later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:279
msgid ""
"\"git rebase -i\" with a series of squash/fixup, when one of the steps "
"stopped in conflicts and ended up getting skipped, did not handle the "
"accumulated commit log messages, which has been corrected.  (merge "
"6ce7afe163 pw/rebase-skip-commit-message-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:283
msgid ""
"Adjust to newer Term::ReadLine to prevent it from breaking the interactive "
"prompt code in send-email.  (merge c016726c2d jk/send-email-with-new-"
"readline later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:286
msgid ""
"Windows updates.  (merge 0050f8e401 ds/maintenance-on-windows-fix later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:290
msgid ""
"Correct use of lstat() that assumed a failing call would not clobber the "
"statbuf.  (merge 72695d8214 st/mv-lstat-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.42.0.txt:329
msgid ""
"Other code cleanup, docfix, build fix, etc.  (merge 51f9d2e563 sa/doc-ls-"
"remote later to maint).  (merge c6d26a9dda jk/format-patch-message-id-unleak "
"later to maint).  (merge f7e063f326 ps/fetch-cleanups later to maint).  "
"(merge e4cf013468 tl/quote-problematic-arg-for-clarity later to maint).  "
"(merge 20025fdfc7 tz/test-ssh-verifytime-fix later to maint).  (merge "
"e48a21df65 tz/test-fix-pthreads-prereq later to maint).  (merge 68b51172e3 "
"mh/commit-reach-get-reachable-plug-leak later to maint).  (merge aeee1408ce "
"kh/use-default-notes-doc later to maint).  (merge 3b8724bce6 jc/test-"
"modernization later to maint).  (merge 447a3b7331 jc/test-modernization-2 "
"later to maint).  (merge d57fa7fc73 la/doc-interpret-trailers later to "
"maint).  (merge 548afb0d9a la/docs-typofixes later to maint).  (merge "
"3744ffcbcd rs/doc-ls-tree-hex-literal later to maint).  (merge 6c26da8404 mh/"
"credential-erase-improvements later to maint).  (merge 78e56cff69 tz/lib-gpg-"
"prereq-fix later to maint).  (merge 80d32e84b5 rj/leakfixes later to "
"maint).  (merge 0a868031ed pb/complete-diff-options later to maint).  (merge "
"d4f28279ad jc/doc-hash-object-types later to maint).  (merge 1876a5ae15 ks/"
"t4205-test-describe-with-abbrev-fix later to maint).  (merge 6e6a529b57 jk/"
"fsck-indices-in-worktrees later to maint).  (merge 3e81b896f7 rs/packet-"
"length-simplify later to maint).  (merge 4c9cb51fe7 mh/doc-credential-"
"helpers later to maint).  (merge 3437f549dd jr/gitignore-doc-example-markup "
"later to maint).  (merge 947ebd62a0 jc/am-parseopt-fix later to maint).  "
"(merge e12cb98e1e jc/branch-parseopt-fix later to maint).  (merge d6f598e443 "
"jc/gitignore-doc-pattern-markup later to maint).  (merge a2dad4868b jc/"
"transport-parseopt-fix later to maint).  (merge 68cbb20e73 jc/parse-options-"
"show-branch later to maint).  (merge 3821eb6c3d jc/parse-options-reset later "
